schema: "0.4"
id: npl-prism-30-review-detail
type: image
quality: high

# NoizuPromptLingo collaboration — Review Detail: pixel-anchored x/y overlay comments
# on a target screenshot, compiled into a pass/fail/changes verdict.
# Theme tenets: luminous frosted glass, cool violet→cyan spectrum gradient, Sora
# geometric type, 16px radius; the annotated screenshot is the focal canvas.
# Palette: violet #7c3aed, cyan #06b6d4, fuchsia #d946ef, canvas #f7f8ff, ink #1a1730.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a
    PREMIUM visual-review surface inside a modern AI product. Polished and focused —
    a central annotated screenshot flanked by frosted-glass panels floating over a pale
    spectrum mesh. Comment pins and the verdict action use the theme's spectrum accents
    with discipline. Clean geometric sans-serif (Sora), no serif.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity UI mockup of the REVIEW DETAIL (overlay annotation) screen of
    NoizuPromptLingo (route /app/[orgId]/reviews/[id]).

    OVERALL LAYOUT (three regions): a slim LEFT app nav rail (achromatic glass), a
    dominant CENTER SCREENSHOT OVERLAY CANVAS, and a RIGHT ~340px column holding the
    comment marker list and the verdict compiler — over a pale near-white canvas
    (#f7f8ff) with a soft blurred violet/cyan spectrum mesh glowing at the edges.

    HEADER BAND (frosted glass): review title in Sora 700, a breadcrumb back to Reviews,
    a small "Open · 3 unresolved" status chip, and a primary "Compile verdict" button
    (violet→cyan gradient, soft glow) at the right.

    SCREENSHOT OVERLAY CANVAS (center, the hero): a large rounded frame (16px) showing a
    target UI SCREENSHOT (a mockup of some product screen being reviewed) sitting on a
    soft glass mat. Pinned on top are several OVERLAY COMMENT PINS — numbered circular
    markers (1,2,3) in the violet primary, each x/y-anchored to a specific point on the
    screenshot. ONE pin is active/open with a small dark rounded comment popover anchored
    to it: an author dot + name, a 1–2 line comment, and a reply field — given a soft
    violet focus ring. The active pin has a subtle spectrum glow.

    RIGHT TOP — COMMENT MARKER LIST: a glass panel listing all pins as rows (numbered dot
    + first line of each comment + author dot + resolved/open state), the active one
    highlighted with a violet edge; a filter for open/resolved.

    RIGHT LOWER — VERDICT COMPILER PANEL: a frosted glass card titled "Verdict" that
    aggregates the open comments into a decision — three selectable options as segmented
    pills: "Pass" (emerald), "Changes requested" (amber), "Fail" (rose), each a flat
    opaque semantic tint; a short summary line ("3 open comments") and a "Compile"
    primary button (violet→cyan gradient).

    PALETTE & TYPE: cool near-white canvas + soft spectrum mesh at edges; ink #1a1730
    text; the violet(#7c3aed)→cyan(#06b6d4) gradient only on primary buttons, glass edges,
    and pin/active accents; verdict options are flat opaque semantic chips. Sora
    everywhere, no serif.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: 16px radius on the canvas frame and panels, pill controls,
    translucent frosted glass with gradient-sheen edges and violet-tinted soft shadows;
    the screenshot canvas is the crisp focal object. Luminous, premium, focused.

    MOOD: premium, precise, collaborative. A visual-review tool that feels modern and
    luminous while keeping the annotated screenshot perfectly legible.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, gradient body text, gradient status chips, rainbow tie-dye buttons, illegible screenshot, neon-on-black cyberpunk"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Matches key components — Screenshot Overlay Canvas with pinned x/y Overlay Comment Pins (one open), Comment Marker List sidebar, Verdict Compiler Panel with pass/changes/fail options"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Prism frosted-glass panels over a spectrum mesh, violet→cyan gradient on primary actions/pins/edges only, flat opaque verdict chips, Sora type, 16px radius; the screenshot canvas is crisp and focal"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Clear focal screenshot with anchored pins + right-side marker list and verdict compiler, plausible real-product layout"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, legible pins/labels and screenshot, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "comment pins not anchored to the screenshot, or no open comment popover"
    - "gradient status chips, gradient body text, or rainbow chrome"

tags: [npl-prism, NoizuPromptLingo, screen-mockup, collaboration]
